NEEDCIO -- programs that want Microware's cio, and how to run them==================================================================These are NOT broken and NOT damaged.  They were compiled the ordinary way forthe era -- Microware C's `cc -qixm`, where -i tells the linker to use the `cio`trap handler instead of linking stdio in.  Give them cio and they work.TESTED: all 78 were run with cio+csl+math present.  71 RUN, and those        71 are what is in these two directories.  The seven that did NOT        run have been moved to /dd/CMDS/BROKEN -- see DOC/STATUS.That is the same bar the rest of this disk is held to, just with one moduleadded.  Nothing here needs fixing; it needs cio.------------------------------------------------------WHERE TO GET cio------------------------------------------------------cio, csl and math ship with Microware's OS-9 SDK.  They are not part of thiscollection; DOC/README-CIO explains how to point the disk at your own.If you have a licensed OS-9/68K SDK or a real OS-9 system disk, copy cio,csl and math from your own CMDS.  That is the supported route and the onlyone this disk endorses.For reference when checking your own copies, the modules this collectionwas built and tested against are:    cio      18058 bytes   (68020 build)    csl      48366 bytes   (68020 build)    math      7798 bytes   (68000 build; works on both)    math881   3220 bytes   (optional, more accurate on a 68881)Put them in /dd/CMDS and these programs run.    chd /dd/CMDS    load cio                 (csl and math too, if a program wants them)------------------------------------------------------WHAT IS HERE------------------------------------------------------/dd/CMDS/NEEDCIO         58 utilities -- RCS, ed, emacs/mg, mtools helpers,                         cp/mv/rm/mkdir, cal, cb, cxref, tail, uniq, unzip,                         strings, chown/chgrp, setterm, sysmon and more.                         See DOC/INDEX for the per-program list./dd/CMDS/GAMES/NEEDCIO   13 games with no surviving source anywhere:                           back       backgammon ("OS-9 BACKGAMMON")                           cribbage   cribbage, offers instructions                           hack       Hack -- the dungeon crawl (data in                                      /dd/GAMES/HACK)                           hotel      hotel management game                           larn       Larn -- roguelike (data in /dd/GAMES/LARN)                           mille      Mille Bornes card game                           piano      play notes; piano <base note> <duration>                           robots     Robots                           tt         "TETRIS FOR TERMINALS"                           ularn      ULarn -- roguelike (data in /dd/GAMES/ULARN)Three programs that USED to live in NEEDCIO -- advent, gnuchess and strings --now also exist as trap-free source builds in /dd/CMDS/GAMES/ and /dd/CMDS/.Those need no module at all; prefer them.  The cio copies are kept forcomparison.------------------------------------------------------THE SEVEN THAT DID NOT RUN -- now in /dd/CMDS/BROKEN------------------------------------------------------Worth keeping and worth someone's attention -- these are not cio problems.  bio          Error 043 (illegal instruction) with cio, csl AND math all  blackjack    loaded.  A real defect in the binary, and there is no source               for either.  A disassembly would be needed to say more.  advent       "Sorry, I can't open advent1.txt".  Needs its text file, which  advent0      is not in this collection.  NOTE: the trap-free `advent` in               /dd/CMDS/GAMES/ is a different, complete build with its data in               /dd/GAMES/ADV -- use that one.  cxref        No output at all.  cxref and delbak may simply be waiting on  delbak       arguments; wysecrack probes for a Wyse terminal that is not  wysecrack    there.  Not investigated further.